        "readable_text": "Content:\nSometimes we can simplify a radical expression by factoring the expression inside the radical.\n\nContent:\nFor instance, let's try to simplify the expression\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{a^2+2a+1}.]\n\nContent:\nWe can begin by factoring the expression under the radical, as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: sqrt(a^{2} + 2a + 1)|=; sqrt(a^{2} + 2 \u22c5 1 \u22c5 a + 1)|=; sqrt((a + 1)^{2})]\n\nContent:\nNow, using the fact that [MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,] we can simplify our expression even further. This gives\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{(a+1)^2} = |a+1|.]"
      },
