        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Given that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x\\geq1,]</span> simplify <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt{4x^2 - 8x + 4}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Given that [MATH: x\\geq1,] simplify [MATH: \\sqrt{4x^2 - 8x + 4}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>To simplify the radical expression, we factor the expression inside the radical and then simplify using the identity <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: sqrt(4x^{2} \u2212 8x + 4)|= sqrt(4 \u22c5 (x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1)); = sqrt(4) \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2 \u22c5 1 \u22c5 x + 1^{2}); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt((x \u2212 1)^{2}); = 2|x \u2212 1|]</span></p><p>Now, since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x \\geq 1,]</span> we have that</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: x-1 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad |x-1| = x-1.]</span></p><p>Therefore, our expression simplifies to <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2(x-1).]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To simplify the radical expression, we factor the expression inside the radical and then simplify using the identity [MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,] as follows:\n\n[MATH: sqrt(4x^{2} \u2212 8x + 4)|= sqrt(4 \u22c5 (x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1)); = sqrt(4) \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2 \u22c5 1 \u22c5 x + 1^{2}); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt((x \u2212 1)^{2}); = 2|x \u2212 1|]\n\nNow, since [MATH: x \\geq 1,] we have that\n\n[MATH: x-1 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad |x-1| = x-1.]\n\nTherefore, our expression simplifies to [MATH: 2(x-1).]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nGiven that [MATH: x\\geq1,] simplify [MATH: \\sqrt{4x^2 - 8x + 4}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo simplify the radical expression, we factor the expression inside the radical and then simplify using the identity [MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,] as follows:\n\n[MATH: sqrt(4x^{2} \u2212 8x + 4)|= sqrt(4 \u22c5 (x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1)); = sqrt(4) \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2 \u22c5 1 \u22c5 x + 1^{2}); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt((x \u2212 1)^{2}); = 2|x \u2212 1|]\n\nNow, since [MATH: x \\geq 1,] we have that\n\n[MATH: x-1 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad |x-1| = x-1.]\n\nTherefore, our expression simplifies to [MATH: 2(x-1).]"
      },
