            "normalized_html": "<p>To simplify the radical expression, we factor the expression inside the radical and then simplify using the identity <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,]</span> as follows:</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\sqrt{4x^4y +12x^4}\n&amp;=  \\sqrt{4x^4(y+3)}  \\[3pt]\n&amp;= \\sqrt{4x^4} \\cdot \\sqrt{y+3}  \\[3pt]\n&amp;= \\sqrt{\\left(2x^2\\right)^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{y+3} \\[3pt]\n&amp;= |2x^2| \\sqrt{y+3}\n}]</span></p><p>Now, since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^2 \\geq0,]</span> we have that</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2x^2 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad |2x^2| = 2x^2.]</span></p><p>Therefore, our expression simplifies to <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2x^2\\sqrt{y + 3}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "To simplify the radical expression, we factor the expression inside the radical and then simplify using the identity [MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,] as follows:\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\sqrt{4x^4y +12x^4}\n&= \\sqrt{4x^4(y+3)} \\[3pt]\n&= \\sqrt{4x^4} \\cdot \\sqrt{y+3} \\[3pt]\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(2x^2\\right)^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{y+3} \\[3pt]\n&= |2x^2| \\sqrt{y+3}\n}]\n\nNow, since [MATH: x^2 \\geq0,] we have that\n\n[MATH: 2x^2 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad |2x^2| = 2x^2.]\n\nTherefore, our expression simplifies to [MATH: 2x^2\\sqrt{y + 3}.]",
