    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nSometimes we can simplify a radical expression by factoring the expression inside the radical.\n\nContent:\nFor instance, let's try to simplify the expression\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{a^2+2a+1}.]\n\nContent:\nWe can begin by factoring the expression under the radical, as follows:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: sqrt(a^{2} + 2a + 1)|=; sqrt(a^{2} + 2 \u22c5 1 \u22c5 a + 1)|=; sqrt((a + 1)^{2})]\n\nContent:\nNow, using the fact that [MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,] we can simplify our expression even further. This gives\n\nContent:\n[MATH: \\sqrt{(a+1)^2} = |a+1|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Simplifying the Square Root of a Perfect Square by Factoring\n\nExample Prompt:\nGiven that [MATH: x\\geq1,] simplify [MATH: \\sqrt{4x^2 - 8x + 4}.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo simplify the radical expression, we factor the expression inside the radical and then simplify using the identity [MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,] as follows:\n\n[MATH: sqrt(4x^{2} \u2212 8x + 4)|= sqrt(4 \u22c5 (x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1)); = sqrt(4) \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2x + 1); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 2 \u22c5 1 \u22c5 x + 1^{2}); = 2 \u22c5 sqrt((x \u2212 1)^{2}); = 2|x \u2212 1|]\n\nNow, since [MATH: x \\geq 1,] we have that\n\n[MATH: x-1 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad |x-1| = x-1.]\n\nTherefore, our expression simplifies to [MATH: 2(x-1).]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nSimplify [MATH: sqrt(x^{2} \u2212 6x + 9).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: |x + 3|]\nb. [MATH: |x \u2212 6|]\nc. [MATH: |3x|]\nd. [MATH: |x \u2212 3|]\ne. [MATH: |3x \u2212 1|]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: sqrt(4x^{2} + 8x + 4) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 2|x \u2212 1|]\nb. [MATH: 2sqrt(x + 1)]\nc. [MATH: \u2212 2|x + 1|]\nd. [MATH: 2|x + 1|]\ne. [MATH: |x + 4|]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nGiven that [MATH: z \u2265 \u2212 1,] simplify [MATH: sqrt(3z^{2} + 6z + 3).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: sqrt(3)z + 1]\nb. [MATH: sqrt(3)(z + 1)]\nc. [MATH: sqrt(3)|z \u2212 1|]\nd. [MATH: 3(z + 1)]\ne. [MATH: sqrt(3)|z + 1|]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Example: Simplifying a Square Root by Factoring a Higher Order Polynomial\n\nExample Prompt:\nSimplify [MATH: \\sqrt{4x^4y +12x^4} .]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo simplify the radical expression, we factor the expression inside the radical and then simplify using the identity [MATH: \\sqrt{a^2} = |a|,] as follows:\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\sqrt{4x^4y +12x^4}\n&= \\sqrt{4x^4(y+3)} \\[3pt]\n&= \\sqrt{4x^4} \\cdot \\sqrt{y+3} \\[3pt]\n&= \\sqrt{\\left(2x^2\\right)^2} \\cdot \\sqrt{y+3} \\[3pt]\n&= |2x^2| \\sqrt{y+3}\n}]\n\nNow, since [MATH: x^2 \\geq0,] we have that\n\n[MATH: 2x^2 \\geq 0 \\quad \\Longrightarrow\\quad |2x^2| = 2x^2.]\n\nTherefore, our expression simplifies to [MATH: 2x^2\\sqrt{y + 3}.]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: sqrt(27a^{5} + 18a^{3} \u2212 9a^{2}) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3asqrt(3a^{3} + 2a + 1)]\nb. [MATH: |3a|(3a^{3} + 2a \u2212 1)]\nc. [MATH: |3a|sqrt(6a^{3} + 4a \u2212 2)]\nd. [MATH: |3a|sqrt(3a^{3} + 2a \u2212 1)]\ne. [MATH: |3a|sqrt(6a^{3} + 2a \u2212 1)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: sqrt(9x^{4} + 12x^{2} + 4) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: 3x^{2} + 2]\nb. [MATH: 9x^{4} \u2212 2]\nc. [MATH: sqrt(3x^{2} + 2)]\nd. [MATH: |3x^{2} \u2212 2|]\ne. [MATH: |9x^{4} + 2|]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Example: Simplifying the Square Root of a Rational Expression\n\nExample Prompt:\nSimplify [MATH: \\sqrt{ \\dfrac{x^2-4x+4}{x^2+6x+9} }.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nTo simplify the expression, we first factor the numerator and denominator under the radical:\n\n[MATH: sqrt((x^{2} \u2212 4x + 4)/(x^{2} + 6x + 9))|= sqrt((x^{2} + 2 \u22c5 x \u22c5 (\u2212 2) + (\u2212 2)^{2})/(x^{2} + 2 \u22c5 x \u22c5 3 + 3^{2})); = sqrt(((x \u2212 2)^{2})/((x + 3)^{2}))]\n\nThen, by applying the quotient rule for radicals and the rules of absolute value, we get\n\n[MATH: sqrt(((x \u2212 2)^{2})/((x + 3)^{2}))|= (sqrt((x \u2212 2)^{2}))/(sqrt((x + 3)^{2})); = (|x \u2212 2|)/(|x + 3|); =|(x \u2212 2)/(x + 3)|.]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\n[MATH: sqrt((t^{2} + 4t + 4)/((12 \u2212 t)^{2})) =]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: |(t + 2)/(12 \u2212 t)|]\nb. [MATH: |(2t)/(12 \u2212 t)|]\nc. [MATH: |(t + 1)/(12 \u2212 t)|]\nd. [MATH: |(t + 12)/(t \u2212 2)|]\ne. [MATH: |(t + 4)/(6 \u2212 t)|]\n\n---\n\nItem 11 \u2014 Question 7\n\nPrompt:\nSimplify [MATH: sqrt((a^{2} \u2212 6a + 9)/(a^{2} + 10a + 25)).]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: |(a \u2212 3)/(a + 5)|]\nb. [MATH: |(a^{2} \u2212 9)/(a + 5)|]\nc. [MATH: |(a \u2212 6)/(a + 5)|]\nd. [MATH: |(a \u2212 6)/(a \u2212 3)|]\ne. [MATH: |(a \u2212 3)/(a + 10)|]"
  }
